      "author": {
        "id": 1096713
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-31T17:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "...are to also avoid memory leaks here.  Note that if `mPolicyParamterMgr` has already been allocated, we leak that here.  And since the destructor doesn\u0027t handle this field, this new instance here also leaks.\n\nIf we switch to `std::unique_ptr`, then we\u0027d make this:\n\n```\nmPolicyParameterMgr \u003d std::make_unique\u003cParameterManagerWrapper\u003e();\n```\n\nThat would destruct any preexisting instance stored in `mPolicyParameterMgr`, avoiding a leak of that.  And this new instance would also be destroyed when this class instance is destructed.",
      "revId": "07d755f6ba627fa32d42c1d0491b22f2d4e1acdf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
