        "id": 1096713
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-31T17:54:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "...make this:\n\n```\nstd::unique_ptr\u003cParameterManagerWrapper\u003e mPolicyParameterMgr;\n```\n\nWe\u0027d need to then also add `#include \u003cmemory\u003e` for this header.\n\nI suggest this because it looks like this field is a private member of this class, we never pass the pointer itself out of this class, and don\u0027t expect its contents to live beyond the life of the instance of this class.  I don\u0027t have deep context on this code, so if my assumptions here are wrong, then we should avoid this.\n\nBut assuming we do this, the advantages, besides making sure this is initialized to `nullptr` by default...",
